Right, that error happens because it runs twice. You can replace `index.js` with the following to not see the error:
```js
console.log("RUNNING");
exports.File = 2;
require("./1");


```

A minimal reproduction:

```js
// index.mjs
import "./dep.cjs";
```
```js
// dep.cjs
require("./dep.cjs");
console.log("RUNNING");
```

Running `node index.mjs` logs twice but it should log once.
